 "explanation": "This couplet explains the relationship between effort (tāḷāṇmai) and benevolence (vēḷāṇmai). The poet states that the proud privilege of being able to help others (vēḷāṇmai ennuñ cerukku) can only abide or be sustained within the noble quality of relentless effort and perseverance (tāḷāṇmai ennum takaimai). Without hard work and the wealth it brings, one cannot experience the joy of generosity. Thus, active exertion is the foundation of all charity.",
